        "text": "Secure Shell\nThe SSH protocol is a secure connection that allows you to execute commands\nremotely on a Linux host (in this case, Kali). By default, the SSH is a TCP pro-\ntocol that works on port 22 by default. There are two ways to connect to a\nremote SSH server:\nI\nI Using a username/password credentials\nI\nI Using public/private keys (passwordless)",
